WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.048 --> 00:00:09.559
"Uh . . . I was just . . . ," Ally stammered.

2
00:00:09.560 --> 00:00:14.281
"This isn't a changing room!" the woman snapped, stepping into the room.

3
00:00:14.282 --> 00:00:16.692
"This is Dr. Lloyd's private office.

4
00:00:16.693 --> 00:00:21.771
You should have found somewhere else to get ready for the costume contest."

5
00:00:21.772 --> 00:00:28.115
Ally almost laughed. "She thinks this is a costume!" she thought.

6
00:00:28.116 --> 00:00:32.722
"So sorry!" Ally scurried for the door.

7
00:00:32.723 --> 00:00:36.477
"You'd better hurry." The woman's voice softened slightly.

8
00:00:36.478 --> 00:00:40.335
"I think the costume contest began a few minutes ago."

9
00:00:40.336 --> 00:00:44.366
"Oh, I'm not entering the contest," Ally said.

10
00:00:44.367 --> 00:00:50.025
"Why not? There's a hundred-dollar prize, and you've got the best costume here."

11
00:00:50.026 --> 00:00:57.297
Before Ally could say anything else, the woman led her out of the office and took her to the main exhibit hall.

12
00:00:57.298 --> 00:01:04.338
Sure enough, a group of humans in costumes stood onstage while two judges walked around, inspecting them.

13
00:01:04.339 --> 00:01:12.644
"If we put an asteroid sticker on your back, that means you advance to the next round!" a judge called out.

14
00:01:12.645 --> 00:01:22.298
"Get on up there!" Dr. Lloyd's assistant gently pushed Ally up.

15
00:01:22.299 --> 00:01:26.056
Ally scooted to the back, behind the other contestants.

16
00:01:26.057 --> 00:01:32.423
She started to sneak off the stage, but one of the judges had spotted her.

17
00:01:32.424 --> 00:01:41.026
"Your costume definitely earns you a spot in the next round!" The judge slapped an asteroid sticker on her.

18
00:01:41.027 --> 00:01:48.219
Ally gulped. "Now I'll never be able to sneak away," she thought.

19
00:01:48.220 --> 00:01:55.318
Soon the contest was down to Ally and a kid dressed as Martian Man.

20
00:01:55.319 --> 00:02:01.201
Ally shook her head. She'd been to Mars once on a peace mission with her parents.

21
00:02:01.202 --> 00:02:05.343
And this kid didn't look anything like a real Martian.

22
00:02:05.344 --> 00:02:08.511
"I don't want to be mean," Ally thought.

23
00:02:08.512 --> 00:02:12.249
"But my costume is so much more authentic."

24
00:02:12.250 --> 00:02:17.445
She did a quick dance move to entertain the audience, and several humans clapped and cheered.

25
00:02:17.446 --> 00:02:24.371
Ally grinned. She hadn't wanted to enter the contest, and she definitely needed to go look for those parts.

26
00:02:24.372 --> 00:02:29.792
But a part of her was having fun. "This contest is like a fashion show," she thought.

27
00:02:29.793 --> 00:02:33.093
"And I'm definitely going to win that cash prize!"

28
00:02:33.094 --> 00:02:36.598
Everyone was eagerly waiting for the winner to be announced.

29
00:02:36.599 --> 00:02:41.205
As the judges huddled together, talking, Ally looked out at the spectators again.

30
00:02:41.206 --> 00:02:47.928
"Oh no!" she thought, spotting her friends. She covered her face. "What if they recognize me?"

31
00:02:47.929 --> 00:02:53.105
But the only one looking at her was Mateo. And he didn't even blink.

32
00:02:53.106 --> 00:02:55.702
At last a judge stepped forward.

33
00:02:55.703 --> 00:03:02.262
"We saw a lot of wonderful costumes today, but there's one that truly stands out.

34
00:03:02.263 --> 00:03:08.113
The winner of the Sandville UFO Convention costume contest is . . ."

35
00:03:08.114 --> 00:03:10.837
A drumroll sounded over the speakers.

36
00:03:10.838 --> 00:03:13.575
Ally stood up taller and fluffed her tentacles.

37
00:03:13.576 --> 00:03:18.462
She wanted to look good and take an Astralian bow when she accepted the prize.

38
00:03:18.463 --> 00:03:23.861
The drumroll ended and the judge said, "Martian Man!"

39
00:03:23.862 --> 00:03:27.649
"What?" Ally felt like she'd been punched.

40
00:03:27.650 --> 00:03:31.143
Several seconds passed before she understood what had just happened.

41
00:03:31.144 --> 00:03:36.733
She'd lost the alien costume contest!

42
00:03:36.734 --> 00:03:40.558
"Ridiculous!" she thought, stomping offstage.

43
00:03:40.559 --> 00:03:44.292
"Humans are so ignorant about other beings in the universe!"

44
00:03:44.293 --> 00:03:53.493
Ally felt angry, but she had a bigger problem—she had to get back into Dr. Lloyd's office.

45
00:03:53.494 --> 00:03:57.738
In the gallery Dr. Lloyd was still talking.

46
00:03:57.739 --> 00:04:04.424
"I've finally achieved a breakthrough in my efforts to communicate with extraterrestrials."

47
00:04:04.425 --> 00:04:10.739
He placed a small black box with a blinking light on the podium.

48
00:04:10.740 --> 00:04:15.365
It was the one Ally had seen in the cabinet.

49
00:04:15.366 --> 00:04:18.694
"My beacons have been sending signals out into space.

50
00:04:18.695 --> 00:04:22.500
They are specially designed to attract aliens to Earth.

51
00:04:22.501 --> 00:04:25.970
And I have proof that my experiment finally worked."

52
00:04:25.971 --> 00:04:30.002
"What?" Ally stared at the screen in horror as Dr. Lloyd played a video.

53
00:04:30.003 --> 00:04:36.411
It showed her escape pod approaching Earth.

54
00:04:36.412 --> 00:04:43.114
"I believe this spaceship landed somewhere in Sandville, and it's still here," Dr. Lloyd announced.

55
00:04:43.115 --> 00:04:45.468
"And I intend to find it!"

56
00:04:45.469 --> 00:04:48.351
Everyone gasped, including Ally.

57
00:04:48.352 --> 00:04:52.487
"How do the beacons work?" someone asked.

58
00:04:52.488 --> 00:05:00.401
"Through advanced technology, the beacons send a signal to communicate to the spaceship that there's something here it needs," Dr. Lloyd explained.

59
00:05:00.402 --> 00:05:07.851
"It could be food, fuel, or even spare parts. But of course, that's just a trick to lure the ship here."

60
00:05:07.852 --> 00:05:16.186
"A trick?" Ally stood, stunned. "I was tricked into landing on Earth?" she thought.

61
00:05:16.187 --> 00:05:26.083
Did that mean she wouldn't find any parts or fuel here?

62
00:05:26.084 --> 00:05:32.256
Tears slipped down her cheeks as she ran out of the gallery and retrieved her meld medallion.

63
00:05:32.257 --> 00:05:39.820
She slipped it over her head and was about to leave the museum when she heard a gasp behind her.

64
00:05:39.821 --> 00:05:42.829
"Ally?"

